ugarcane states reported, reflecting Karnataka's tropical multi-irrigation cropping pattern.\n- **Net irrigation water requirement by technique (Karnataka, mm/year)**: furrow irrigation 1,878 mm; skip furrow 1,408 mm; sprinkler 1,325 mm; drip 1,186 mm — showing drip irrigation can reduce net water requirement by roughly 37% compared to conventional furrow irrigation for the same crop water demand.\n\n### Water-economizing methods\n1. **Skip-furrow/alternate furrow irrigation**: one row is skipped and irrigation applied only to alternate furrows, saving 30–40% water without reducing cane productivity.", "farmer": "How deep should each irrigation be for sugarcane?"}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "How deep should each irrigation be for sugarcane?"}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.9124}, "retrieved": [{"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information", "score": 0.9124, "via": "original"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Summary", "score": 0.9017, "via": "original"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Key Facts", "score": 0.8958, "via": "original"}, {"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information", "score": 0.891, "via": "original"}], "raw_answer": "Irrigation water depth generally ranges from 7–8 centimeters but varies based on specific field condition as detailed above.", "claims": ["supported: Irrigation water depth generally ranges from 7–8 centimeters"], "unsupported": [], "final_answer": "Irrigation water depth generally ranges from 7–8 centimeters but varies based on specific field condition as detailed above.", "fact_check": "checked", "fact_check_seconds": 0.74, "groq_calls": [{"purpose": "fact_check", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prom